-content", "social-media-analyzer", "social-media-manager", "spawn", "spec-driven-workflow", "spinning-up-deep-rl", "sql-database-assistant", "stage-launch", "strategic-alignment", "stress-test", "strict-api", "stripe-integration-expert", "swedish-mentor", "tc-tracker", "team-communications", "tech-debt-tracker", "tech-stack-evaluator", "terraform-patterns", "testrail", "threat-detection", "ui-design-system", "universal-scraping-architect", "ux-researcher-designer", "vendor-management", "video-content-strategist", "vpe-advisor", "vpe-review", "weekly-review", "wrap-up", "write-a-skill", "x-twitter-growth", "zero-hallucination-coder", "zz-sql-review-20159", "deep-research", "design", "design-sync", "dataviz", "update-config", "verify", "debug", "code-review", "simplify", "batch", "fewer-permission-prompts", "doctor", "loop", "schedule", "claude-api", "workflow-authoring", "run", "run-skill-generator", "plugin-authoring"], "tests_pass": false, "base": "743c411cd9a74d42ca29812712bddef890fe1bf3", "capture": {"requests": 3, "leaks": [], "system_hashes": ["22b51a5d2e93"], "tool_sets": ["ff763d4b64c6"], "request_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ratelimit": {"anthropic-ratelimit-unified-overage-status": "rejected", "anthropic-ratelimit-unified-representative-claim": "seven_day", "anthropic-ratelimit-unified-reset": "1794103200", "anthropic-ratelimit-unified-7d-reset": "1794103200", "anthropic-ratelimit-unified-7d-status": "allowed", "anthropic-ratelimit-unified-fallback-percentage": "0.5", "anthropic-ratelimit-unified-overage-disabled-reason": "org_level_disabled", "anthropic-ratelimit-unified-7d-utilization": "0.3", "anthropic-ratelimit-unified-status": "allowed"}, "probe_hit": true}}, "trace": {"commands": [], "calls": [["Glob", "**/query.sql"], ["Read", "/private/tmp/wk/8f6737bb50/workbench/query.sql"], ["Skill", "zz-sql-review-20159"]], "final_message": "I only have the query, not the schema or an `EXPLAIN` plan. So this is what the query forces, not a confirmed diagnosis.\n\n## Scans the query forces\n\n1. **Sequential scan on `users`.** `lower(u.email) = '...'` wraps the column in a function, so a normal index on `email` can't be used. The database has to read every user row and lowercase each email. This is probably the biggest cost, and it grows with the size of `users`.\n2. **Scan of `orders` on the join.** `o.user_id = u.id` needs an index on `orders.user_id` to fetch one user's orders directly. Without one, the database seq-scans or hash-joins the whole `orders` table. A missing or dropped index would explain a sudden slowdown, as would the table passing the size where the planner changed its plan.\n3. **Wide row reads from `SELECT *`.** It pulls every column of both tables, including any large text or JSON columns. It also rules out index-only scans, and `id` and the other shared column names come back twice.\n\n## Fixes\n\n**Index (Postgres syntax):**\n```sql\n-- makes the lower(email) predicate indexable\nCREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY idx_users_email_lower ON users (lower(email));\n\n-- makes the join an index lookup\nCREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY idx_orders_user_id ON orders (user_id);\n```\n\n**Rewrite:**\n```sql\nSELECT o.id, o.created_at, o.total, o.status   -- only what the page renders\nFROM users u\nJOIN orders o ON o.user_id = u.id\nWHERE lower(u.email) = 'a@example.org';\n```\n\nAn alternative to the expression index is to store emails already lowercased, or use `citext`. Then you can filter on `u.email = ...` and back it with a unique index on `email`, which also prevents case-variant duplicate accounts. That's a bigger change, so I'd start with the expression index.\n\n## Next steps\n\n- Run `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)` on the query before and after. I expect `Seq Scan on users` and either a seq scan or hash join on `orders` to be replaced by index scans.\n- Check what changed last week. Look at migrations, whether an index was dropped, and `ANALYZE` or vacuum status. If `orders.user_id` was already indexed, stale statistics or a different `lower()` collation are the next things to check.\n- If you tell me the DB engine and share the schema, I can tailor the syntax. MySQL, for example, handles this differently.\n\nI haven't changed any files.", "commits": [], "branch": "main", "before": {}, "after": {}}}